principals are "alice", "bob", "data2_admin", "unlisted".
resources are "data1", "data2", "unlisted".
actions are "read", "unlisted", "write".
roles are "alice", "bob", "data2_admin".
principal "alice" has roles "alice", "data2_admin".
principal "bob" has roles "bob".
principal "data2_admin" has roles "data2_admin".
state "available" initially false.
deny when principal has role "alice" and resource is "data2" and action is "write".
allow when principal has role "alice" and resource is "data1" and action is "read" then set state "available" to not state "available".
allow when principal has role "bob" and resource is "data2" and action is "write" then set state "available" to not state "available".
allow when principal has role "data2_admin" and resource is "data2" and action is "read" then set state "available" to not state "available".
allow when principal has role "data2_admin" and resource is "data2" and action is "write" then set state "available" to not state "available".
otherwise deny.
